# Nexus v2.0 — Technical Implementation Plan

## Architecture Overview

### Current Architecture
```
cmd/nexus/          → TUI entry point (bubbletea)
cmd/nexus-gui/      → GUI entry point (ebiten)
internal/
  config/           → YAML config, connection types, SSH import
  crypto/           → AES-256-GCM encryption
  health/           → TCP health checking
  ipc/              → Unix socket TUI↔GUI bridge
  launcher/         → Protocol-specific launch strategies
  session/          → SSH (managed + standard), Telnet
  tui/              → Bubbletea app, views, keys, styles
  gui/              → Ebiten app, tabs, RDP, VNC, input
```

### Target Architecture (v2.0)
```
cmd/nexus/          → TUI entry point
cmd/nexus-gui/      → GUI entry point (unchanged)
internal/
  config/           → Config loading, connection types, SSH import
  crypto/           → Encryption (unchanged)
  health/           → Health checking (enhanced)
  ipc/              → IPC bridge (unchanged)
  launcher/         → Launch strategies (enhanced with hooks)
  session/          → Protocol sessions (enhanced with recording, port forwarding)
  store/            → NEW: Storage abstraction (YAML + SQLite backends)
  theme/            → NEW: Color scheme system with semantic colors
  tui/
    app.go          → Root model (enhanced with modal system)
    mode.go         → NEW: Modal system (Normal/Insert/Visual/Command)
    motion.go       → NEW: Vim motion engine (count, operator, motion)
    leader.go       → NEW: Leader key handler + which-key popup
    whichkey.go     → NEW: Which-key popup view
    table.go        → NEW: Custom k9s-style table (replaces bubbles/table)
    tree.go         → NEW: Folder tree view
    finder.go       → NEW: Telescope-style fuzzy finder
    search.go       → NEW: Incremental search with highlight
    pane.go         → NEW: Split pane management
    command.go      → Enhanced command palette with history + aliases
    filter.go       → Enhanced filter with regex/fuzzy/tag/group modes
    statusbar.go    → Enhanced with mode indicator + position
    header.go       → Enhanced k9s-style header
    keys.go         → Enhanced keybindings
    styles.go       → Replaced by theme system
    marks.go        → NEW: Vim marks + jump list
    undo.go         → NEW: Undo/redo stack
    visual.go       → NEW: Visual mode selection
    pulse.go        → NEW: Health dashboard (pulse view)
    notes.go        → NEW: Connection notes viewer
    recorder.go     → NEW: Session recording controls
    bulk.go         → NEW: Bulk operation handler
    notification.go → NEW: Notification system
    (existing views retained: list, detail, form, help, confirm, log, sessions)
  import/           → NEW: Import engines (CSV, JSON, PuTTY, mRemoteNG)
  export/           → NEW: Export engines (CSV, JSON, YAML)
  hooks/            → NEW: Connection lifecycle hooks
  audit/            → NEW: Audit logging
  vault/            → NEW: Credential vault abstraction
  template/         → NEW: Connection templates
```

## Implementation Phases

### Phase 1: Foundation Layer (Blocks everything else)

**P1.1 — Theme System** [Prerequisite for all UI work]
- Create `internal/theme/` package
- Define `Theme` struct with semantic color map (bg, fg, accent, error, warning, success, info, subtle, highlight, cursor, selection, border, header, muted)
- Define mode colors, protocol colors, status colors
- Implement TokyoNight Storm as default
- Implement built-in themes: catppuccin-mocha, dracula, gruvbox-dark, nord
- Theme loading from YAML skin file
- Replace all hardcoded colors in styles.go with theme references
- Add `:theme` command to switch themes at runtime

**P1.2 — Modal System** [Prerequisite for all keybinding work]
- Create `internal/tui/mode.go`
- Define `Mode` type: Normal, Insert, Visual, Command
- Mode state machine with transition rules
- Mode change events (ModeChangedMsg)
- Integration with App.Update() — route keys differently per mode
- Esc always transitions to Normal
- Mode indicator rendering in statusbar (color-coded per mode)
- Cursor shape changes per mode (block for Normal, line for Insert)

**P1.3 — Vim Motion Engine** [Prerequisite for navigation and operators]
- Create `internal/tui/motion.go`
- Count accumulator: digit keys build count prefix (e.g., `5` then `j` = move 5 down)
- Motion types: line (j/k), page (Ctrl+d/u/f/b), screen (H/M/L), absolute (gg/G), search (n/N), char (f/F)
- Operator types: delete (d), yank (y), change (c)
- Operator + motion composition: pending operator state, apply on motion
- Doubled operator = operate on current item (dd, yy, cc)
- Visual mode integration: operator applies to selection
- Reset on Esc or invalid key

**P1.4 — k9s-Style Table** [Replaces bubbles/table for main view]
- Create `internal/tui/table.go`
- Custom table renderer (not using bubbles/table)
- Features: column headers with sort indicators, row striping, cursor bar highlight
- Sort by column with Shift+key shortcuts
- Wide mode toggle (Ctrl+W) for additional columns
- Column auto-sizing with minimum widths
- Status column with colored indicators
- Latency column with color gradient
- Age column with human-readable durations
- Integrates with motion engine for navigation (count+j/k, gg, G, H/M/L, Ctrl+d/u)

**P1.5 — k9s-Style Layout Overhaul**
- Redesign header: logo left, config info right, k9s menu-style hotkey bar
- Add title bar below header: view name + item count + active filter
- Redesign statusbar: mode (color) | stats | flash | position (N/M)
- Command/filter input at very bottom (below statusbar)
- Crumbs bar showing navigation path

### Phase 2: Core Interaction (Depends on Phase 1)

**P2.1 — Leader Key + Which-Key**
- Create `internal/tui/leader.go` and `internal/tui/whichkey.go`
- Space key enters leader-pending state
- 500ms timeout triggers which-key popup
- Which-key popup: semi-transparent overlay showing key groups
- Nested navigation: pressing a group key updates popup to sub-group
- All leader key groups from spec (c, f, s, g, i, e, t, v, h, p, o, ?)
- Dismiss on Esc or valid action key

**P2.2 — Incremental Search Enhancement**
- Create `internal/tui/search.go`
- `/` activates forward search, `?` reverse search
- Incremental filtering as user types
- Search highlighting in table cells (matched text styled differently)
- Filter modes: regex, inverse (!), fuzzy (-f), tag (-t), group (-g)
- n/N for cycling matches
- Search history (up/down arrows)
- * and # for word-under-cursor search

**P2.3 — Visual Mode**
- Create `internal/tui/visual.go`
- `V` enters line-visual (multi-select contiguous range)
- `v` toggles selection on current item
- Visual selection rendered with highlight style
- Selected count shown in statusbar
- Operators work on visual selection (d, y, tag operations)
- Esc exits visual, clears selection

**P2.4 — Marks + Jump List**
- Create `internal/tui/marks.go`
- m{a-z} sets mark at current position (view + cursor row)
- '{a-z} jumps to mark
- Jump list: every navigation push (view change, search jump, mark jump) recorded
- Ctrl+o / Ctrl+i navigate jump list back/forward
- `:marks` shows all marks in overlay
- `` `` jump to position before last jump

**P2.5 — Command Palette Enhancement**
- Enhance `internal/tui/command.go`
- Command history persisted to disk (~/.config/nexus/history)
- Up/Down arrows cycle history
- Tab completion with cycling through matches
- New commands: sort, filter, mark, pulse, theme, template, version, export, import
- Command aliases in config (e.g., c = connect, q = quit)
- Argument parsing: `:connect user@host`, `:sort name`, `:filter -t production`
- Range syntax: `:1,10 delete`

**P2.6 — Undo/Redo**
- Create `internal/tui/undo.go`
- Operation stack recording all destructive changes
- Operations: ConnectionAdded, ConnectionDeleted, ConnectionEdited, ConnectionMoved, TagAdded, TagRemoved
- `u` undoes last operation (restores previous state)
- `Ctrl+r` redoes
- Stack depth: 50
- Flash message on undo/redo showing what changed

### Phase 3: Session Power Features (Can parallel with Phase 2)

**P3.1 — SSH Jump Host / ProxyJump**
- Add `ProxyJump []string` and `ProxyCommand string` to Connection config
- Update SSH session to use ProxyJump (multi-hop)
- Health checker: check each hop independently, aggregate status
- Table indicator column for jump host connections (⇢ symbol)
- Form fields for jump host configuration
- SSH config import: parse ProxyJump and ProxyCommand directives

**P3.2 — SSH Port Forwarding**
- Add `PortForwards []PortForward` to Connection config
- PortForward struct: Type (local/remote/dynamic), LocalAddr, RemoteAddr
- Implement in SSH session: dial forwarded ports on connect
- Port forward management view (list active, add, remove)
- Active forwards shown in session detail panel

**P3.3 — Connection Lifecycle Hooks**
- Create `internal/hooks/` package
- Hook definition: event (pre-connect/post-connect/pre-disconnect/post-disconnect), command string, on-failure (abort/warn/ignore)
- Hook execution with timeout (30s default)
- Hook output captured in event log
- Hook config per-connection and inheritable from folders
- Config schema: hooks: [{event, command, on_failure}]

**P3.4 — Session Recording**
- Create recording module in `internal/session/`
- Asciicast v2 format (JSON events with timing)
- Recording toggled per-connection (config field: record: optional/required/disabled)
- Storage directory configurable (~/.local/share/nexus/recordings/ default)
- Metadata: connection ID, start time, duration, bytes written
- Recording list view (`:recordings`)
- Retention policy: auto-delete after N days

**P3.5 — Quick Connect**
- `<leader>cc` or `:connect` opens input prompt
- Parse formats: `user@host`, `user@host:port`, `ssh://user@host:port`
- Auto-detect protocol from port or URI scheme
- Connect immediately without saving
- Post-connect option: "Save this connection? (y/n)" flash prompt
- Recent quick connects stored in memory (last 20)

### Phase 4: Organization (Depends on Phase 1 table, can parallel Phase 2-3)

**P4.1 — Folder Tree View**
- Create `internal/tui/tree.go`
- Tree data structure: Node{name, children, connections, collapsed, depth}
- Folder definition in config: `folders:` section with nested structure
- Tree renderer: indentation + expand/collapse icons (▸ collapsed, ▾ expanded)
- Vim fold keys: za toggle, zo open, zc close, zR open all, zM close all
- Folder CRUD: `:mkdir name`, `:rmdir name`, `:mv connection folder`
- View toggle: `<leader>vt` switches between table and tree view
- Folder inheritance: connections inherit folder settings (credentials, hooks, jump host)

**P4.2 — Favorites & Recent**
- Add `favorite bool` and `last_connected_at time` and `connect_count int` to Connection
- Toggle favorite: `<leader>ff` or `:fav`
- View favorites: `<leader>fv` or `:favorites` (filters list to favorites only)
- View recent: `<leader>fr` or `:recent` (sorted by last_connected_at)
- View frequent: `:frequent` (sorted by connect_count)
- Favorite indicator in table (★ column)
- Pin favorites to top (toggle in settings)

**P4.3 — Connection Templates**
- Create `internal/template/` package
- Template definition in config: `templates:` section
- Template struct: name, protocol, default fields (host pattern, port, username, identity_file, hooks, jump_host)
- Built-in templates: ssh-standard, ssh-jumphost, rdp-windows, vnc-linux, telnet-network
- Template selection in add form (dropdown)
- `:template create`, `:template list`, `:template edit`, `:template delete`
- Template application: fill form fields from template, user overrides

**P4.4 — Tags Enhancement**
- Tag autocomplete in filter and command mode
- Boolean tag filter: `:tag web AND prod`, `:tag web OR api`, `:tag NOT staging`
- Tag cloud view (`:tags`): all tags with connection counts, sorted by count
- Bulk tag in visual mode: select connections, `:tag add production`
- Tag column in table (when in wide mode)

**P4.5 — Bracket Navigation**
- `]c`/`[c` next/previous connection (simple, already j/k but semantically distinct in filtered views)
- `]g`/`[g` next/previous group boundary
- `]e`/`[e` next/previous offline/error connection
- `]s`/`[s` next/previous active session
- `]f`/`[f` next/previous favorite

### Phase 5: Data Layer (Can parallel Phase 3-4)

**P5.1 — Storage Abstraction**
- Create `internal/store/` package
- `Store` interface: List, Get, Create, Update, Delete, Search, Close
- `YAMLStore` implementation (wraps existing config.go)
- `SQLiteStore` implementation (modernc.org/sqlite — pure Go, no CGO)
- Config option: `storage: yaml` or `storage: sqlite`
- SQLite schema: connections, folders, tags, templates, audit_log, settings tables
- Full-text search via FTS5
- Automatic migration: `:migrate sqlite` converts YAML to SQLite

**P5.2 — Import Engines**
- Create `internal/import/` package
- `Importer` interface: Parse(reader) ([]Connection, error), Preview() string
- CSVImporter: field mapping wizard (header detection, column assignment)
- JSONImporter: RDM-compatible JSON format
- SSHConfigImporter: enhanced (already exists, promote to package)
- Import preview: show table of what will be created/updated
- Merge strategies: skip, overwrite, rename (append -2, -3)
- Import via `:import csv path`, `:import json path`, `:import ssh`

**P5.3 — Export Engines**
- Create `internal/export/` package
- `Exporter` interface: Export(connections, writer, options) error
- CSVExporter, JSONExporter, YAMLExporter
- Options: include_credentials (requires master password), encrypt_export
- Export scope: all, filtered, selected (visual mode), group
- `:export csv /path`, `:export json /path --no-creds`

**P5.4 — Credential Vault**
- Create `internal/vault/` package
- `Vault` interface: Get(id), Set(id, secret), Delete(id), List()
- `InternalVault` — current AES-256-GCM encrypted storage
- `PassVault` — integration with `pass` (password-store)
- `OnePasswordVault` — integration with `op` CLI
- `BitwVault` — integration with `bw` CLI (Bitwarden)
- Credential entries: reusable across connections (credential_id reference)
- SSH key management: list keys in ~/.ssh/, generate new keys, import keys
- SSH agent integration: detect ssh-agent, add keys on connect

### Phase 6: Monitoring & Polish (Depends on Phase 5 for audit storage)

**P6.1 — Pulse View (Health Dashboard)**
- Create `internal/tui/pulse.go`
- Dashboard layout: summary cards + tables
- Cards: total connections, online, offline, degraded, active sessions
- Group health table: group name, total, online, offline, avg latency
- Protocol distribution: text bar chart (SSH: ████████ 45, RDP: ████ 12)
- Recent activity: last 10 connections with timestamps
- Latency table: connections sorted by latency (worst first)
- Accessible via `:pulse` or `<leader>hp`

**P6.2 — Audit Log**
- Create `internal/audit/` package
- Events: connect, disconnect, error, credential_viewed, credential_used, config_changed
- SQLite storage (audit.db, separate from connections)
- Log viewer: searchable, filterable by date/event/connection
- Retention policy: auto-prune after N days (default 90)
- Export: `:audit export csv /path`

**P6.3 — Connection Notes**
- Add `notes string` field to Connection
- Notes editor in detail view (simple multiline textarea)
- Markdown rendering in viewport
- Quick note: `<leader>n` opens note editor for current connection
- Notes searchable in global search
- Pre-connect README: if connection has notes and `show_readme: true`, display before connecting

**P6.4 — Custom Fields**
- Add `custom_fields map[string]string` to Connection
- Custom field definitions in config: `field_definitions: [{name, type, description}]`
- Visible in detail view
- Searchable
- Displayable as table columns (configurable)

**P6.5 — Telescope Fuzzy Finder**
- Create `internal/tui/finder.go`
- Three-panel layout: prompt, results, preview
- Scoring algorithm: character position weighting + consecutive bonus + start bonus
- Live update as user types
- Preview panel: connection detail for highlighted item
- Multi-select with Tab
- Pickers: connections, sessions, tags, groups, recent, favorites
- `<leader>ff` or `Ctrl+p` to activate

**P6.6 — Notification System Enhancement**
- State change notifications: connection came online/went offline
- Session timeout warnings (configurable)
- Credential expiry warnings
- Notification history in log
- Optional desktop notifications via notify-send

**P6.7 — Bulk Operations**
- Visual mode select + operator
- Range commands: `:1,10 delete`, `:1,10 tag add prod`
- Bulk connect: connect all selected/filtered
- Progress indicator for multi-item operations
- Confirmation for destructive bulk operations

